    "created_at": "2018-01-30T04:58:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-30T04:58:50Z",
    "body": "The problem is caused by the \"1.\" being line-wrapped to the start of the next line. *In general*, no, you can't get around this; lines starting with \"1.\" or similiar kicking off a list immediately is a common feature of all valid markdown processors, and is explicitly captured in the CommonMark spec.\r\n\r\nHowever, you're in luck! CommonMark explicitly calls out *this exact case* (the \"1.\" being the *only* content on the line) and makes it *not* start a list, which means Bikeshed is buggy.  I'll file an issue and fix soon.\r\n\r\n(In general, if a line that *looks* like it should start a list is immediately preceded by paragraph lines, it won't start a list if the list-marker is the only content on that line, or if it's a numbered list other than \"1.\".)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
